{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity"},"abstract":[{"text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Entity"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An entity is one thing in your game or simulation. It has no data of its own: a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores the components it holds, and the handle is how you refer to it. You get a handle by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spawning an entity, and you pass it back to the world to read and change its components:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let hero = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Ada\"), Health(current: 100))","","print(world[Name.self, of: hero].value)","\/\/ Prints \"Ada\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A handle is a small value, cheap to copy and store, for example in a component that refers to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"another entity. It holds two numbers: the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of the slot the entity occupies in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world, and the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of that slot. When an entity is despawned, the world can reuse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its slot for a new entity with the next generation, so a handle kept past its entity’s despawn","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"stale","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": it never names the entity that took the slot.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let first = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","world.despawn(first)","let second = world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 1))","","print(first, second)","\/\/ Prints \"0:0 0:1\"","print(world.contains(first))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities are ordered by slot, then by generation.","type":"text"}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/_(_:_:)"]},{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(index:generation:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/Comparable-Implementations","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"E